Mezery
******

.[perex]
Sekce `spacing` rozhoduje o mezerách na řádku: kolem operátorů, za čárkou, uvnitř závorek, mezi jménem funkce a závorkou, za klíčovým slovem, kolem `->` a `::`, v deklaraci typu a v komentáři.

U mezery je hodnotou ukázka kódu: konstrukce napsaná přesně s tou mezerou, kterou chcete, v jednoduchých uvozovkách. Čte se nejlíp, protože říká přesně to, co uvidíte v kódu:

```neon
spacing:
	concatenation: '$a.$b'
	arrowFunction: 'fn ($x) => $x'
	cast: '(int) $x'
	catchType: 'catch (A|B $e)'
```

Ukázku DressCode nečte jako kód, jen ji porovná s ukázkami, které klíč zná; neznámá ukázka je chyba, která vypíše ty známé. Každý klíč řídí jen mezeru, kterou jmenuje: v `'fn ($x) => $x'` je to mezera za `fn`, mezery kolem `=>` patří jinému klíči. Ukázka platí přesně, takže širší mezeru nepustí; víc mezer může zůstat jen tam, kde zarovnává sloupce a dovolí to skupina `spacing.alignment`. Vnitřek závorek se nepíše ukázkou, ale slovem: skupina `spacing.padding` říká pro každý druh závorek, jestli v nich mezera být musí (`required`), nebo nesmí (`forbidden`).

```php .[before]
$label = 'Item '.$name . ' x'.$count;  // Expected no whitespace before the `.` operator. // Expected no whitespace after the `.` operator.
$double = fn($x) => $x * 2;  // Expected a single space after the `fn` keyword.
$id = (int)$row['id'];  // Expected a single space after the cast.
```

```php .[after]
$label = 'Item '.$name.' x'.$count;
$double = fn ($x) => $x * 2;
$id = (int) $row['id'];
```

Mezera nikdy nerozhoduje o zlomu řádku: mezera kolem operátoru, který stojí na zlomu, je věc odsazení a sekce [multiline |multiline], ne téhle. Kde víc mezer zarovnává sloupce, rozhodují parametry skupiny `spacing.alignment` (binární operátor, čárka, ternární operátor a komentář za kódem), jestli zarovnání smí zůstat; DressCode sloupce sám nikdy nezarovnává.


spacing.keyword
===============

The space after a keyword followed by code on its line, `return`, `new`, `if`, `function`, a modifier and the words of the head of a class among them, and around a keyword continuing a statement, `else`, `catch`, `finally`, the `while` of a `do`, `as`, `insteadof` and the `use` of a closure, which stay on the line of what is before them.

- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `required`, psr12 `required`, nette `required`, symfony `required`, laravel `required` · pokrývá `function_declaration`, `single_space_around_construct`, `Generic.WhiteSpace.LanguageConstructSpacing`, `PSR12.Classes.AnonClassDeclaration`, `PSR12.Traits.UseDeclaration`, `PSR2.Classes.ClassDeclaration`, `PSR2.Classes.ClassDeclaration.SpaceBeforeKeyword`, `PSR2.ControlStructures.SwitchDeclaration`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ControlSignature`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ForEachLoopDeclaration`, `Squiz.Functions.FunctionDeclaration` .[decision-facts]


spacing.anonymousClass
======================

The space between `class` and the arguments of an anonymous class.

- `'new class ($a)'`: a single space before the arguments
- `'new class($a)'`: no space before the arguments
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'new class ($a)'`, psr12 `'new class ($a)'`, nette `'new class ($a)'`, symfony `'new class($a)'`, laravel `'new class($a)'` · pokrývá `class_definition`, `PSR12.Classes.AnonClassDeclaration` .[decision-facts]


spacing.comment.marker
======================

The space after the marker of a comment and before the closing one, unless another `/` or `*` follows the marker, as in a `////` ruler; doc comments are the matter of the phpDoc rules.

- `'// text'`: a single space after the marker
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `'// text'`, symfony `'// text'`, laravel `'// text'` · pokrývá `PhpCsFixerCustomFixers/comment_surrounded_by_spaces`, `single_line_comment_spacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.comment.afterCode
=========================

The whitespace before a comment that follows code on its line.

- `'$a; // text'`: at least one space
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `'$a; // text'`, symfony `'$a; // text'`, laravel `keep` .[decision-facts]


spacing.alignment.comment
=========================

The whitespace wider than a single space before a comment following code, aligning a column of comments; alignment is never made.

- `forbidden`: never there, more whitespace collapsing to a single space
- `optional`: there or not, as the author wrote it

Výchozí `optional` · standardy: perCs `optional`, psr12 `optional`, nette `optional`, symfony `optional`, laravel `optional` .[decision-facts]


spacing.switchCase
==================

The whitespace before the colon of a `case`.

- `'case 1:'`: none before the colon
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'case 1:'`, psr12 `'case 1:'`, nette `'case 1:'`, symfony `'case 1:'`, laravel `'case 1:'` · pokrývá `switch_case_space`, `PSR2.ControlStructures.SwitchDeclaration`, `PSR2.ControlStructures.SwitchDeclaration.SpaceBeforeColonCASE` .[decision-facts]


spacing.binaryOperator
======================

The spaces around a binary operator, an assignment, `instanceof`, `=>` and the `=` of a default included, `.` being `spacing.concatenation`; at a line break an operator takes no space on the side of the break, an assignment and `=>` stay on the line of what is before them, and `instanceof` and a comparison keep what follows them on their line, unless the line would grow too wide.

- `'$a + $b'`: a single space around
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'$a + $b'`, psr12 `'$a + $b'`, nette `'$a + $b'`, symfony `'$a + $b'`, laravel `'$a + $b'` · pokrývá `binary_operator_spaces`, `PSR12.Operators.OperatorSpacing`, `Squiz.WhiteSpace.LogicalOperatorSpacing`, `Squiz.WhiteSpace.OperatorSpacing` .[decision-facts]

Týká se aritmetických, porovnávacích, logických a bitových operátorů, `??`, přiřazení včetně `+=` a `??=`, `instanceof`, `=>` a `=` výchozí hodnoty. Tečka má vlastní klíč `concatenation`, protože o ní se styly rozcházejí.

```neon
spacing:
	binaryOperator: '$a + $b'
```

```php .[before]
$total=$price*$count;  // Expected at least one space before the `=` operator. // Expected at least one space after the `=` operator. // Expected at least one space before the `*` operator. // Expected at least one space after the `*` operator.
$label = $count>1 ? 'items' : 'item';  // Expected at least one space before the `>` operator. // Expected at least one space after the `>` operator.
$map = ['a'=>1, 'b' => 2];  // Expected at least one space before the double arrow. // Expected at least one space after the double arrow.
$aligned   = 1;
$alsoFine  = 2;
```

```php .[after]
$total = $price * $count;
$label = $count > 1 ? 'items' : 'item';
$map = ['a' => 1, 'b' => 2];
$aligned   = 1;
$alsoFine  = 2;
```

Poslední dva řádky zůstaly: zarovnání mezerami dovoluje výchozí hodnota `spacing.alignment.binaryOperator`.


spacing.concatenation
=====================

The space around the concatenation operator, unless it sits at a line break.

- `'$a . $b'`: a single space around
- `'$a.$b'`: no space around
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'$a . $b'`, psr12 `'$a . $b'`, nette `'$a . $b'`, symfony `'$a.$b'`, laravel `'$a.$b'` · pokrývá `concat_space`, `PSR12.Operators.OperatorSpacing`, `Squiz.Strings.ConcatenationSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.alignment.binaryOperator
================================

The whitespace wider than a single space around an operator, aligning a column of assignments `=` or of array items `=>`; alignment is never made.

- `forbidden`: never there, more whitespace collapsing to a single space
- `spaces`: spaces aligning a column staying, tabs not
- `tabs`: tabs aligning a column staying, spaces not
- `optional`: there or not, as the author wrote it

Výchozí `spaces` · standardy: perCs `spaces`, psr12 `spaces`, nette `spaces`, symfony `forbidden`, laravel `forbidden` · pokrývá `binary_operator_spaces`, `PSR12.Operators.OperatorSpacing`, `Squiz.WhiteSpace.LogicalOperatorSpacing`, `Squiz.WhiteSpace.OperatorSpacing` .[decision-facts]

```neon
spacing:
	binaryOperator: '$a + $b'
	alignment:
		binaryOperator: forbidden
```

```php .[before]
$aligned   = 1;  // Expected a single space before the `=` operator.
$alsoFine  = 2;  // Expected a single space before the `=` operator.
```

```php .[after]
$aligned = 1;
$alsoFine = 2;
```


spacing.objectOperator
======================

The whitespace around the object operator.

- `'$a->b()'`: none around
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `'$a->b()'`, symfony `'$a->b()'`, laravel `'$a->b()'` · pokrývá `object_operator_without_whitespace`, `Squiz.WhiteSpace.ObjectOperatorSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.doubleColon
===================

The whitespace around the double colon.

- `'Foo::bar()'`: none around
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `'Foo::bar()'`, symfony `keep`, laravel `'Foo::bar()'` · pokrývá `no_space_around_double_colon`, `Squiz.WhiteSpace.ScopeKeywordSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.unaryOperator
=====================

The whitespace between a unary operator other than `!` and its operand, which stay on one line, and inside a variable variable, `$$a` and `${'a'}`.

- `'-$x'`: no space after the operator
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'-$x'`, psr12 `'-$x'`, nette `'-$x'`, symfony `'-$x'`, laravel `'-$x'` · pokrývá `unary_operator_spaces`, `Generic.WhiteSpace.IncrementDecrementSpacing`, `Squiz.WhiteSpace.OperatorSpacing.Unary` .[decision-facts]


spacing.logicalNot
==================

The whitespace between `!` and its operand, which stay on one line.

- `'!$x'`: no space after the operator
- `'! $x'`: a single space after the operator
- seznam těchto ukázek, kde projde každá a kód, který neodpovídá žádné, se napíše podle první
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `['!$x', '! $x']`, psr12 `['!$x', '! $x']`, nette `'!$x'`, symfony `'!$x'`, laravel `'! $x'` · pokrývá `not_operator_with_successor_space`, `not_operator_without_successor_space`, `unary_operator_spaces`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Operators.NegationOperatorSpacing`, `Squiz.WhiteSpace.OperatorSpacing.Unary` .[decision-facts]


spacing.cast
============

The space between a cast and its operand, which stays on the line of the cast.

- `'(int) $x'`: a single space after the cast
- `'(int)$x'`: no space after the cast
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'(int) $x'`, psr12 `'(int) $x'`, nette `'(int) $x'`, symfony `'(int) $x'`, laravel `'(int) $x'` · pokrývá `cast_spaces` .[decision-facts]


spacing.reference
=================

The whitespace between `&` and its operand.

- `'&$x'`: none between
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'&$x'`, psr12 `'&$x'`, nette `'&$x'`, symfony `'&$x'`, laravel `keep` · pokrývá `SlevomatCodingStandard.PHP.ReferenceSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.spread
==============

The whitespace between `...` and its operand.

- `'...$x'`: none between
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'...$x'`, psr12 `'...$x'`, nette `'...$x'`, symfony `'...$x'`, laravel `keep` · pokrývá `SlevomatCodingStandard.Operators.SpreadOperatorSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.ternary
===============

The whitespace around `?` and `:` of a ternary, and around `?:` as a whole, unless the operator sits at a line break.

- `'$a ? $b : $c'`: whitespace around `?` and `:`
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'$a ? $b : $c'`, psr12 `'$a ? $b : $c'`, nette `'$a ? $b : $c'`, symfony `'$a ? $b : $c'`, laravel `'$a ? $b : $c'` · pokrývá `ternary_operator_spaces`, `PSR12.Operators.OperatorSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.alignment.ternary
=========================

The whitespace wider than a single space around `?` and `:`, aligning a column; alignment is never made.

- `forbidden`: never there, more whitespace collapsing to a single space
- `optional`: there or not, as the author wrote it

Výchozí `optional` · standardy: perCs `optional`, psr12 `optional`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `optional`, laravel `optional` · pokrývá `ternary_operator_spaces`, `PSR12.Operators.OperatorSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.declare
===============

The whitespace inside a `declare` statement.

- `'declare(strict_types=1)'`: none inside
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'declare(strict_types=1)'`, psr12 `'declare(strict_types=1)'`, nette `'declare(strict_types=1)'`, symfony `'declare(strict_types=1)'`, laravel `'declare(strict_types=1)'` · pokrývá `declare_equal_normalize`, `declare_parentheses`, `PSR12.Files.DeclareStatement` .[decision-facts]


spacing.call
============

The whitespace between the name of a function and its parenthesis, of a call and of a declaration alike.

- `'foo($a, $b)'`: no space before the parenthesis
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'foo($a, $b)'`, psr12 `'foo($a, $b)'`, nette `'foo($a, $b)'`, symfony `'foo($a, $b)'`, laravel `'foo($a, $b)'` · pokrývá `function_declaration`, `no_spaces_after_function_name`, `Generic.Functions.FunctionCallArgumentSpacing.SpaceBeforeOpenBracket`, `PSR2.Methods.FunctionCallSignature`, `Squiz.Functions.FunctionDeclaration` .[decision-facts]


spacing.namedArgument
=====================

The whitespace around the colon of a named argument.

- `'foo(name: $x)'`: none before the colon, a single space after
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'foo(name: $x)'`, psr12 `keep`, nette `'foo(name: $x)'`, symfony `'foo(name: $x)'`, laravel `keep` · pokrývá `SlevomatCodingStandard.Functions.NamedArgumentSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.typeDeclaration
=======================

The whitespace of a type declaration, which stays on one line with what it describes: none inside a type, a single space between a type and the name it declares, `): int` for a return type and `enum Suit: string` for a backing type.

- `'?int $x'`: none inside a type, a single space before the name
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'?int $x'`, psr12 `'?int $x'`, nette `'?int $x'`, symfony `'?int $x'`, laravel `'?int $x'` · pokrývá `compact_nullable_type_declaration`, `return_type_declaration`, `type_declaration_spaces`, `types_spaces`, `PSR12.Functions.NullableTypeDeclaration`, `PSR12.Functions.ReturnTypeDeclaration`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Classes.BackedEnumTypeSpacing`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.ParameterTypeHintSpacing`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.ReturnTypeHintSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.catchType
=================

The space around the bar between the types of a `catch`.

- `'catch (A | B $e)'`: a single space around the bar
- `'catch (A|B $e)'`: no space around the bar
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'catch (A|B $e)'`, psr12 `'catch (A | B $e)'`, nette `'catch (A|B $e)'`, symfony `'catch (A|B $e)'`, laravel `'catch (A|B $e)'` .[decision-facts]


spacing.attribute
=================

The whitespace inside the brackets of an attribute group and before the parenthesis of its arguments, and the single space between two groups on a line and after the last one.

- `'#[Foo($a)]'`: none inside the brackets, none before the parenthesis
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'#[Foo($a)]'`, psr12 `keep`, nette `'#[Foo($a)]'`, symfony `'#[Foo($a)]'`, laravel `keep` · pokrývá `attribute_block_no_spaces` .[decision-facts]


spacing.comma
=============

The whitespace around a comma, which stays on the line of what is before it, a line ending after it being free.

- `'$a, $b'`: none before, a single space after
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'$a, $b'`, psr12 `'$a, $b'`, nette `'$a, $b'`, symfony `'$a, $b'`, laravel `'$a, $b'` · pokrývá `no_whitespace_before_comma_in_array`, `whitespace_after_comma_in_array`, `Generic.Functions.FunctionCallArgumentSpacing`, `Squiz.Functions.FunctionDeclarationArgumentSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.alignment.comma
=======================

The whitespace wider than a single space after a comma, aligning the columns of a table; alignment is never made.

- `forbidden`: never there, more whitespace collapsing to a single space
- `spaces`: spaces aligning a column staying, tabs not
- `tabs`: tabs aligning a column staying, spaces not
- `optional`: there or not, as the author wrote it

Výchozí `tabs` · standardy: perCs `forbidden`, psr12 `forbidden`, nette `tabs`, symfony `optional`, laravel `optional` · pokrývá `no_whitespace_before_comma_in_array`, `whitespace_after_comma_in_array`, `Generic.Functions.FunctionCallArgumentSpacing`, `Squiz.Functions.FunctionDeclarationArgumentSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.openBrace
=================

The space before the brace or the body a structure opens on the line of its head.

- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `required`, psr12 `required`, nette `required`, symfony `required`, laravel `required` · pokrývá `Squiz.ControlStructures.ControlSignature` .[decision-facts]


spacing.alternativeSyntax
=========================

The space before the colon of the alternative syntax and of a label, and the single space between it and the end keyword of an empty body, `if ($a): endif;`.

- `'if ($a):'`: no space before the colon
- `'if ($a) :'`: a single space before the colon
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'if ($a):'`, psr12 `'if ($a):'`, nette `'if ($a):'`, symfony `'if ($a):'`, laravel `keep` .[decision-facts]


spacing.body
============

The space inside the braces of a body whose code stands on their line, of a function, a closure, a property hook and an anonymous class, and of abbreviated property hooks, `{ get; set; }`; none inside a pair of braces with nothing between them whose empty form `braces.emptyBody` does not decide.

- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `required`, psr12 `required`, nette `required`, symfony `required`, laravel `keep` .[decision-facts]


spacing.import
==============

The space around the braces of a group use, which hug the names.

- `'use Acme\{Foo, Bar};'`: no space around the braces
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'use Acme\{Foo, Bar};'`, psr12 `'use Acme\{Foo, Bar};'`, nette `'use Acme\{Foo, Bar};'`, symfony `'use Acme\{Foo, Bar};'`, laravel `keep` .[decision-facts]


spacing.arrowFunction
=====================

The space between `fn` and its parenthesis.

- `'fn($x) => $x'`: no space before the parenthesis
- `'fn ($x) => $x'`: a single space
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'fn($x) => $x'`, psr12 `keep`, nette `'fn($x) => $x'`, symfony `'fn ($x) => $x'`, laravel `'fn ($x) => $x'` · pokrývá `function_declaration`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Functions.ArrowFunctionDeclaration` .[decision-facts]


spacing.anonymousFunction
=========================

The space between the `function` of a closure and its parenthesis.

- `'function($x)'`: no space before the parenthesis
- `'function ($x)'`: a single space
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'function ($x)'`, psr12 `'function ($x)'`, nette `'function ($x)'`, symfony `'function ($x)'`, laravel `'function ($x)'` · pokrývá `function_declaration`, `Squiz.Functions.MultiLineFunctionDeclaration` .[decision-facts]


spacing.padding.argument
========================

The whitespace inside the parentheses of the arguments of a call, of `new` and of an attribute, and of `isset()`, `unset()`, `empty()` and `eval()`.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `forbidden`, psr12 `forbidden`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `forbidden`, laravel `forbidden` · pokrývá `function_declaration`, `no_spaces_inside_parenthesis`, `spaces_inside_parentheses`, `PSR12.Classes.AnonClassDeclaration`, `PSR12.ControlStructures.ControlStructureSpacing`, `PSR2.ControlStructures.ControlStructureSpacing`, `PSR2.Methods.FunctionCallSignature`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ForEachLoopDeclaration`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ForLoopDeclaration` .[decision-facts]


spacing.padding.parameter
=========================

The whitespace inside the parentheses of the parameters of a function, a method, a closure, an arrow function and a property hook.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `forbidden`, psr12 `forbidden`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `forbidden`, laravel `forbidden` · pokrývá `function_declaration`, `no_spaces_inside_parenthesis`, `spaces_inside_parentheses`, `PSR12.Classes.AnonClassDeclaration`, `PSR12.ControlStructures.ControlStructureSpacing`, `PSR2.ControlStructures.ControlStructureSpacing`, `PSR2.Methods.FunctionCallSignature`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ForEachLoopDeclaration`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ForLoopDeclaration` .[decision-facts]


spacing.padding.closureUse
==========================

The whitespace inside the parentheses of the `use` of a closure.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `forbidden`, psr12 `forbidden`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `forbidden`, laravel `forbidden` · pokrývá `function_declaration`, `no_spaces_inside_parenthesis`, `spaces_inside_parentheses`, `PSR12.Classes.AnonClassDeclaration`, `PSR12.ControlStructures.ControlStructureSpacing`, `PSR2.ControlStructures.ControlStructureSpacing`, `PSR2.Methods.FunctionCallSignature`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ForEachLoopDeclaration`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ForLoopDeclaration` .[decision-facts]


spacing.padding.controlStructure
================================

The whitespace inside the parentheses of `if`, `elseif`, `while`, `for`, `foreach`, `switch`, `match` and `catch`.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `forbidden`, psr12 `forbidden`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `forbidden`, laravel `forbidden` · pokrývá `function_declaration`, `no_spaces_inside_parenthesis`, `spaces_inside_parentheses`, `PSR12.Classes.AnonClassDeclaration`, `PSR12.ControlStructures.ControlStructureSpacing`, `PSR2.ControlStructures.ControlStructureSpacing`, `PSR2.Methods.FunctionCallSignature`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ForEachLoopDeclaration`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ForLoopDeclaration`, `Squiz.WhiteSpace.ControlStructureSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.padding.grouping
========================

The whitespace inside the parentheses grouping an expression, `($a + $b) * $c`.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `forbidden`, psr12 `forbidden`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `forbidden`, laravel `forbidden` · pokrývá `function_declaration`, `no_spaces_inside_parenthesis`, `spaces_inside_parentheses`, `PSR12.Classes.AnonClassDeclaration`, `PSR12.ControlStructures.ControlStructureSpacing`, `PSR2.ControlStructures.ControlStructureSpacing`, `PSR2.Methods.FunctionCallSignature`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ForEachLoopDeclaration`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ForLoopDeclaration` .[decision-facts]


spacing.padding.array
=====================

The whitespace inside the brackets or the parentheses of an array.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `forbidden`, laravel `forbidden` · pokrývá `trim_array_spaces`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Arrays.SingleLineArrayWhitespace` .[decision-facts]


spacing.padding.list
====================

The whitespace inside the brackets or the parentheses of a destructuring.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `forbidden`, laravel `forbidden` · pokrývá `trim_array_spaces`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Arrays.SingleLineArrayWhitespace` .[decision-facts]


spacing.padding.offset
======================

The whitespace inside the brackets of an offset access and before them.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `required`: always there
- `exceptLiterals`: a single space around an index other than a string or an integer literal, `$a[ $i ]` but `$a[0]`
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `forbidden`, laravel `forbidden` · pokrývá `no_spaces_around_offset`, `Squiz.Arrays.ArrayBracketSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.semicolon.before
========================

The whitespace before a semicolon, which stays on the line of what it ends.

- `'$a;'`: no space before a semicolon
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `'$a;'`, psr12 `keep`, nette `'$a;'`, symfony `'$a;'`, laravel `'$a;'` · pokrývá `no_singleline_whitespace_before_semicolons`, `PSR12.Traits.UseDeclaration`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ForLoopDeclaration`, `Squiz.WhiteSpace.SemicolonSpacing` .[decision-facts]


spacing.semicolon.after
=======================

The whitespace after a semicolon that more code follows on its line.

- `'for ($i = 0; $i < 5; $i++)'`: a single space after a semicolon
- `keep`: nic se nevynucuje, kód zůstane, jak je

Výchozí `keep` · standardy: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `'for ($i = 0; $i < 5; $i++)'`, symfony `'for ($i = 0; $i < 5; $i++)'`, laravel `'for ($i = 0; $i < 5; $i++)'` · pokrývá `space_after_semicolon`, `Squiz.ControlStructures.ForLoopDeclaration` .[decision-facts]
